PFIM Alembic migrations
=======================

This directory contains the complete executable schema history.
``tests/integration/test_migrations_match_models.py`` verifies that a database
created by all migrations matches the models in ``app/models``.

Run these diagnostic commands from ``backend/`` with the virtual environment
activated:

  python -m alembic -c alembic.ini heads
  python -m alembic -c alembic.ini current
  python -m alembic -c alembic.ini history

A migration changes the database resolved by ``app/config.py``. Before an
upgrade, stop the backend, check the effective ``DATABASE_URL``, and create a
consistent, verified backup. For an operational database, use an explicit
target revision and follow the procedure in ``docs/data-safety.md`` and
``docs/setup.md`` at the project root.

The FastAPI lifespan compares the database's current heads with the heads
distributed here using read-only access. A mismatch blocks startup; it never
automatically runs ``upgrade``, ``stamp``, or ``create_all``.

Do not add columns manually or use ``alembic stamp`` to conceal an unmigrated
schema. Tests and migration rehearsals must use in-memory SQLite, a temporary
file, or an explicitly authorized separate copy, never ``data/pfim.db``.
